    <!-- Master/Sub Model -->
    <string name="master_model_title">Master Model (Memory)</string>
    <string name="master_model_desc">Periodic summarization to compress context, avoid token overflow. Optional.</string>
    <string name="sub_model_title">Sub Model</string>
    <string name="sub_model_desc">Model for action execution. Same as master or independently configured.</string>
    <string name="sub_use_master_config">Use same config as master model</string>
    <string name="master_intent_prompt">First identify user intent: (1) Task - user wants to do something; (2) False wake-up - accidental trigger; (3) Casual chat.\nIf false wake-up or chat: respond friendly and call finish(message=\"...\").\nIf task: generate a task plan and output the first action. You will receive screen descriptions (text from vision model) at each step to guide your decisions.\n\n**Task plan rules**: Each step must be self-contained and specific. For send-message/comment tasks, the plan must include \"type content\", \"tap send button\", and \"verify UI reacted (e.g. message in chat)\". For summarize/view steps use \"current\".\n\n**Important**: Use target for tap actions (e.g. do(action=\"Tap\", target=\"search icon\")), direction for swipe (e.g. do(action=\"Swipe\", direction=\"up\")). No coordinates needed.</string>
    <string name="master_step_prompt">Based on the screen description and task progress below, decide the next action.\nOutput one action at a time.\nIf all tasks complete, call finish(message=\"summary\").\nIf stuck or error, call finish(message=\"error: description\").\n\n**Important**: For send/submit tasks, Tap send after Type, then verify the UI has reacted (e.g. message appears in chat). Only call finish after confirming success. Do NOT finish without verifying.\n\nUpdate task plan status in &lt;think&gt; (&lt;task_plan&gt; with [x] done, [/] in progress, [ ] pending).</string>
